    "body": "In general I think the linking text should be what people will be using when they write the code. Nobody's going to write `somebc <a>browsing context nested through</a> anotherbc`; they'll write `somebc <a>nested through</a> anotherbc` (and will use `for=\"browsing contexts\"` to disambiguate if there are multiple \"nested throughs\" in the ecosystem).\n\nWhereas, people will definitely with `somebc is an <a>ancestor browsing context</a>`.\n",
